    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A western Georgian kingdom ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a> by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagrationi dynasty</a>, separate from 1260 and definitively from 1490.</li><li>It spent over two centuries as an Ottoman tributary, troubled by rebellious <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> and a cruel trade in slaves.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon-i-of-imereti">Solomon I</a> revived it in the eighteenth century, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon-ii-of-imereti">Solomon II</a> and annexed it in 1810.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Two battles fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chikhori-1757">Chikhori</a> shaped Imereti’s history: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrat-iii-of-georgia">Bagrat</a>’s victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-viii-of-georgia">George VIII</a> in 1463 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon-i-of-imereti">Solomon I</a>’s victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1757.</p></aside>
    </section>

